use core
use web/server
use web/script
use def/app.api
use def/site.page
use def/views/site.nav
use def/views/home.view
use def/views/hello.view
use def/views/bmi.view
use def/views/missing.view

// run with:  def-lang run website   then open http://localhost:8000
// settings.toml says how it runs (port, reloading changed files); save it to change them while it runs.
//
// A single page application: each view is an HTML def in def/views/, and the
// page (def/site.page.def) holds them all, with the script that switches views
// without reloading. The views ask the api below for data.
//
//   def/site.page.def       the one page the views live in (HTML)
//   def/app.api.def         what the api runs
//   def/views/*.view.def    one file per view, in HTML
//   def/views/site.nav.def  the links at the top
//   settings.toml           port, everyone, reload, check_every
//
// The web server and the script come from the web library (web/server and
// web/script), installed with def-lang install.

// visits is shared by def/app.api.def; this file sends it
use visits from def/app.api
api "/api/visit" runs count the visit and sends visits, time, today
api "/api/hello" sends greeting
api "/api/bmi" sends bmi, verdict
serve site page at "/"
start the server
